*****************
 Useful Commands
*****************

I'm sure most of these commands will be known by most people but I just had some spare time so I thought i'd compile a list of what I tend to use. 
It is definitely not the difinitive list. There are several others to say the least!


chkdsk - Scans for disk problems without making any changes.
chkdsk /r - Scans for disk problems and repairs corrupted files.
chkdsk /f - For finding and fixing bad sectors.
sfc - Runs a scan for corrupt files and repairs them.
diskpart - Manages disk partitions.
list disk - Displays all the disk drives on the machine.
clean - Removes partitions from a selected disk. 

dir - List directory's files and subdirectory's. 
cd - Use this to change the working directory.
cd / - Navigates to the root directory.
mkdir - Creates a new directory.
rmdir - Removes a directory.
copy - Copies one or more files to a different location.
rename - Kinda self explanatory. 
find - Searches for string in file/files.
del - Deletes a file. (del song.mp4) for example.
tree - Shows the tree of the current directory. (This is pretty cool)
cls - Clears the command line box. (Very usefull after a while!)
clip - Copies an item to the clipboard.

systeminfo - As it suggests really, provides info about the OS, hardware and network.
wmic product get name - Lists all installed programs on the computer.
ver - Shows the OS Version you are running.
driverquery - This will list all the machines installed drivers.
winver - Sees which version of Windows you are running.
tasklist - Displays all running processes.
taskkill - Stops a running task.
powercfg - Shows how your machine is using energy
powercfg/energy - creates a HTML doc with a battery report.
shutdown - pretty self explanatory. Shuts the machine down.

hostname - Displays the computers network name.
ping - Test to see if a network device can be reached. 
getmac - Displays the MAC address of the network card
netstat - This will display open ports and their IP's 
tracert - Great for helping find problems on a network by tracing the path of a packet.
pathping - Basically combines ping and tracert commands.

winget upgrade - Lists all apps, their current version and available upgrades.
winget upgrade --all - upgrades all outdated apps. (Great tool)








